obj/

# Default `dotnet publish` output (App/GitExtensions.Avalonia.csproj sets PublishDir).
dist/

# The settings file the reused core writes at run time. Its folder is named after
# the product (Application.UserAppDataPath -> ProductName), so it appears beside the
# sources whenever the app is started from the build tree — and it was committed by
# accident once, then dirtied the working tree on every run. Both the old name and
# the new one are ignored: a build from an older commit still writes the old folder.
GitNext/
GitExtensions.Avalonia/GitExtensions.settings*
